{"title":"2002 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO\" title=\"2002 USAMO\"> 2002</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"USAMO\">USAMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set with 2002 elements, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/5131fd18229ab805cdb957bda9563d16ffee08d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le N \\le 2^{2002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />.  Prove that it is possible to color every subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> either blue or red so that the following conditions hold:\n</p><p>(a) the union of any two red subsets is red;\n</p><p>(b) the union of any two blue subsets is blue;\n</p><p>(c) there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> red subsets.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle such that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f7adec454ebe970f7dd462f42f733efd6172ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\cot \\frac{A}{2} \\right)^2 + \\left( 2 \\cot \\frac{B}{2} \\right)^2 + \\left( 3 \\cot \\frac{C}{2} \\right)^2 = \\left( \\frac{6s}{7r} \\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"384\" height=\"46\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denote its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semiperimeter\" title=\"Semiperimeter\">semiperimeter</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inradius\" title=\"Inradius\">inradius</a>, respectively.  Prove that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is similar to a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> whose side lengths are all positive integers with no common divisor and determine those integers.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that any monic polynomial (a polynomial with leading coefficient 1) of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with real coefficients is the average of two monic polynomials of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> real roots.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> be the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>.  Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e769732c09eafd5777222570e5c3aba3973c47f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb21cc82bd37243d911f9065df15643ac93f110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^2 - y^2) = xf(x) - yf(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>for all pairs of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> be integers greater than 2.  Prove that there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and a finite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/935c5514187e64b59e60dcedb07f40e000c70455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2, \\ldots, n_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201bdf656d0786716ddc15aa2e1bc9bbdaecd5e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54eeda6a2b7cf6cd1d13ade3c89387cf8b2e9a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_k = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de1ae34acc4ad9b08c69882a11937eebe823bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_in_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5610f0f6b26eb004047146d3580e95563364b6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i + n_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de06b166301e15e67e0e984266544ed6302e241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3><p>\nI have an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> sheet of stamps, from which I've been asked to tear out blocks of three adjacent stamps in a single row or column. (I can only tear along the perforations separating adjacent stamps, and each block must come out of the sheet in one piece.) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> be the smallest number of blocks I can tear out and make it impossible to tear out any more blocks. Prove that there are real constants <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f8227e8e6f5e87f8ff9762baf0e1f00748cd32eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{7} n^2 - cn \\leq b(n) \\leq \\dfrac{1}{5} n^2 + dn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"227\" height=\"37\" /></center><p> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1431ad346632b25a0e7b3f12ebe19723b3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\">USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2002\">2002 USAMO Problems on the Resources page</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO\" title=\"2002 USAMO\">2002 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO\" title=\"2001 USAMO\">2001 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO\" title=\"2003 USAMO\">2003 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017193204\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 237/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1255/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 64/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6143/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.920      1 -total\n 57.63%    6.869      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.32%    4.806      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7430:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017193204 and revision id 224174. Rendering was triggered bec